  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">African elephant taxonomy: Identifying African elephant populations classifications for decision-making and recommendations for conservation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. To collect and analyze genetic data from locations prioritized for research. 2. To compile and synthesise information on the classification of all African elephant populations as forest, savanna, hybrid, and/or unknown based on available genetic, morphological, or other research. 3. To use this research and associated products to engage the AfESG membership in revisiting the AfESG statement on taxonomy, including recommendations. 4. To provide technical information and advice on the conservation and management of Africas elephants in the context of this issue to the following: a. range State government agencies, b. non-governmental organizations, including both international and African-based organisations, c. inter-governmental organizations, and d. non-range State governments; 5. To identify future directions for taxonomic research and related conservation questions.</narrative>
  </description>
